\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Plots summarizing luminosity and data quality reported by the LHC and ATLAS during Run 2 from 2015 to 2018. \ref {fig:ATLAS:PileUp}~Distribution of the mean number of interactions per bunch crossing, $\mu $, weighted by the luminosity. The individual distributions for each year of $pp$ collision data taking during Run 2 are shown. The mean $\mu $ value for each year are given in the legend. \ref {fig:ATLAS:IntLumi}~Cumulative integrated luminosity delivered to and recorded by the ATLAS experiment during Run 2. Data recorded at $\sqrt  {s}=13~\text  {TeV}\xspace  $ during stable beam $pp$ collisions is considered, including special runs for detector calibration. The data sample certified for physics analysis usage is shown in light blue with the \textit  {Good for Physics} label. Figures taken from Ref.~\blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {DAPR-2018-01}.}}{8}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
